{"kind":"assert","text":"User direction after the plan review: schedule estimates must not constrain functionality. Proceed with the complete scope and review as progress is made.\n\nThis narrows the interpretation of my review c31169e9: the scope reductions in finding 5 and the two-lane recommendation in section 13 are advisory suggestions, not approval requirements. I withdraw scope cuts and staffing limits as conditions of approval. Estimates may inform sequencing, dependencies and risk, but must not gate functionality. The arithmetic correction remains factual; the listed estimates total 28.5 engineer-days.\n\nThe Architecture, Security and API correctness requirements in findings 1–4 and 6 remain applicable to the complete scope. Finding 7 calls for accurate evidence and claims. Subsequent reviews will assess delivered progress against the complete intended scope, preserving extensibility and breadth of impact and value for agents and people."}